 in the history of art.","startYear",1503,"startMonth",0,"startDay","endYear",1519,"endMonth","endDay","startSignificance",0.9,"endSignificance",1,"imageUrl","https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Mona_Lisa%2C_by_Leonardo_da_Vinci%2C_from_C2RMF_retouched.jpg/330px-Mona_Lisa%2C_by_Leonardo_da_Vinci%2C_from_C2RMF_retouched.jpg","imageCredit","Image: Mona Lisa / Wikimedia Commons","sourceUrl","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mona_Lisa","cdnId","country",{"_32":80,"_81":82},"subjects",[77],"group",{"_32":74,"_75":76},"user",{"_30":71,"_72":73},"likes","liked",false,"6","username","HistOracle","Renaissance","icon","GiPalette",{"_30":78,"_32":79},"9","art","Italy","continent","Europe","2063","Titian","person","A leading figure of the Venetian school of the Italian Renaissance, celebrated for his innovative use of color and brushwork.","His influence extended beyond his lifetime, shaping the course of Western painting.",1488,1576,8,27,0.8,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Tizian_090.jpg/330px-Tizian_090.jpg","Image: Titian / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Titian",{"_32":80,"_81":82},[100],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":78,"_32":79},"2060","Raphael","An influential painter and architect, known for his harmonious compositions and mastery of perspective.","His works remain pivotal in the study of Renaissance art, celebrated for their beauty and clarity.",1483,4,6,1520,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Raffaello_Sanzio.jpg/330px-Raffaello_Sanzio.jpg","Image: Raphael / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raphael",{"_32":80,"_81":82},[116],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":78,"_32":79},"2061","Michelangelo","A renowned sculptor, painter, and architect, celebrated for his masterpieces in the Renaissance art movement.","His legacy endures through his iconic works, influencing countless artists and shaping the future of Western art.",1475,3,1564,2,18,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Michelangelo_Daniele_da_Volterra_%28dettaglio%29.jpg/330px-Michelangelo_Daniele_da_Volterra_%28dettaglio%29.jpg","Image: Michelangelo / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michelangelo",{"_32":80,"_81":82},[133],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":78,"_32":79},"1165","Nicolaus Copernicus","A Renaissance mathematician and astronomer who formulated a model of the universe that placed the Sun rather than the Earth at its center.","His revolutionary ideas laid the groundwork for modern astronomy and changed the way humanity perceives its place in the cosmos.",1473,19,1543,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Nikolaus_Kopernikus_MOT.jpg/330px-Nikolaus_Kopernikus_MOT.jpg","Image: Nicolaus Copernicus / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicolaus_Copernicus",{"_32":151,"_81":82},[148],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":149,"_32":150},"4","intellectual","Poland","2065","Albrecht Dürer","A German painter, printmaker, and theorist, renowned for his detailed artworks and contributions to the Northern Renaissance.","His legacy is marked by his innovative techniques and influence on subsequent generations of artists.",1471,5,21,1528,0.7,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/D%C3%BCrer_Alte_Pinakothek.jpg/330px-D%C3%BCrer_Alte_Pinakothek.jpg","Image: Albrecht Dürer / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer",{"_32":169,"_81":82},[168],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":78,"_32":79},"Germany","2067","Desiderius Erasmus","A prominent humanist and theologian, he was known for his critical approach to the Church and his advocacy for education and reform.","His death marked the end of an influential career that shaped the intellectual landscape of Europe.",1466,1536,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Holbein-erasmus.jpg/330px-Holbein-erasmus.jpg","Image: Erasmus / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desiderius_Erasmus",{"_32":187,"_81":82},[183,184],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":149,"_32":150},{"_30":185,"_32":186},"7","religion","Netherlands","312","Leonardo da Vinci","An Italian polymath, he is widely considered one of the greatest painters of all time and a key figure of the Renaissance.","His contributions to art, science, and engineering left a lasting impact on various fields.",1452,15,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Francesco_Melzi_-_Portrait_of_Leonardo.png/330px-Francesco_Melzi_-_Portrait_of_Leonardo.png","Unknown author / Wikimedia Commons / Public domain","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leonardo_da_Vinci","images/0e23c80e0c288c9f84db795e85f3b4520fe41f76.webp",{"_32":80,"_81":82},[203,204],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":185,"_72":202},"Kushim",{"_30":205,"_32":206},{"_30":78,"_32":79},"3","culture","992","The Printing Revolution","period","This period marked the transition from manuscript culture to print, significantly impacting literacy and knowledge dissemination.","The period concluded with the establishment of print as a dominant medium for communication, influencing various aspects of society.",1450,1600,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Collage_of_printing.png/330px-Collage_of_printing.png","Image: Printing / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Printing_revolution",{"_32":222,"_81":222},[221],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":185,"_72":202},{"_30":149,"_32":150},"Global","2064","Lorenzo de' Medici","A prominent statesman and patron of the arts, known for his support of artists and intellectuals during the Renaissance.","His contributions to culture and politics significantly shaped Florence's golden age.",1449,1492,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Lorenzo_de_Medici.jpg/330px-Lorenzo_de_Medici.jpg","Image: Lorenzo de' Medici / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lorenzo_de%27_Medici",{"_32":80,"_81":82},[236,237],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":238,"_32":239},{"_30":205,"_32":206},"2","politics","1342","The Invention of the Printing Press","This innovation revolutionized the way information was disseminated, allowing for the mass production of books and the spread of knowledge.","The impact of this invention continues to influence communication and education worldwide.",1440,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/PrintMus_038.jpg/330px-PrintMus_038.jpg","Image: Printing press / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Printing_press",{"_32":169,"_81":82},[252,253],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":205,"_32":206},{"_30":149,"_32":150},"1069","Renaissance Music","The Renaissance marked a rebirth of interest in the arts, leading to innovations in music composition, harmony, and instrumentation.","This period's advancements laid the groundwork for the Baroque era and modern Western music.",1400,0.4,"","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_the_Renaissance",{"_32":82,"_81":82},[266,267],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":205,"_32":206},{"_30":78,"_32":79},"1037","Age of Discovery","This period marked extensive exploration and maritime expansion by European powers, leading to the discovery of new lands and sea routes.","The era concluded as colonial empires were established, fundamentally altering global trade and interactions.","https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Theatrum_Orbis_Terrarum%2C_by_Abraham_Ortelius%2C_World%2C_1572.jpg/330px-Theatrum_Orbis_Terrarum%2C_by_Abraham_Ortelius%2C_World%2C_1572.jpg","Image: Age of Discovery / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Age_of_Discovery",{"_32":222,"_81":222},[279],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":71,"_32":280},"maritime","2069","Donatello","A prominent sculptor of the early Renaissance, known for his innovative techniques and expressive forms in marble and bronze.","His legacy continues to influence artists and sculptors, marking him as a pivotal figure in the development of Renaissance art.",1386,12,13,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Five_Famous_Men_of_the_Florentine_Renaissance%2C_Donatello_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Five_Famous_Men_of_the_Florentine_Renaissance%2C_Donatello_%28cropped%29.jpg","Image: Donatello / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donatello",{"_32":80,"_81":82},[295],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":78,"_32":79},"59","The Renaissance","A cultural movement that began in Italy, emphasizing art, science, and humanism.","The Renaissance marked the transition from the Middle Ages to modernity in Europe.",1300,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/El_nacimiento_de_Venus%2C_por_Sandro_Botticelli.jpg/330px-El_nacimiento_de_Venus%2C_por_Sandro_Botticelli.jpg","Sandro Botticelli / Wikimedia Commons / Public domain","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Renaissance","images/3b452139b2065790575c41a7544589b40a860984.webp",{"_32":80,"_81":82},[309,310],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":185,"_72":202},{"_30":149,"_32":150},{"_30":78,"_32":79},[],"subject",[],[],"yearStart",-300000,"yearEnd",2025,"search","sortBy",true,7]
